o know how to play clubs. "],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["ls","sc"],["md","0,h8765,,h3cq65"],["hs","ws"],["hs","wh"],["at","On the above layout, for example, West will show up with 4 spades, 5 hearts, "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["ls","wh"],["hs","wd"],["at","and at least 3 diamonds. "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["hs","wc"],["at","West can have no more than 1 club and "],["pg",""],["ls","wc"],["hc","cq"],["at","East can be finessed for the @CQ with certainty."],["pg",""],["lc","cq"],["md","0,c5,,s6"],["hs","ws"],["hs","wh"],["nt","\nOn the above layout, West will count out to 3 spades, 5 hearts, "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["ls","wh"],["hs","wd"],["at","and at least 3 diamonds. "],["pg",""],["md","0,cq,,c5"],["ls","wd"],["hs","wc"],["at","There is no certain play as  West might have a doubleton @CQ. "],["pg",""],["md","0,c5,,cq"],["ls","wc"],["hc","cq"],["at","However, the odds heavily favour playing East for the @CQ "],["pg",""],["lc","cq"],["hs","ec"],["at","as he is known to hold at least 5 clubs."],["pg",""],["ls","ec"],["md","0,s6h3cq6,,h8765"],["hs","ws"],["hs","wh"],["nt","\nOn the actual layout, West will be known to have 4 spades, 2 hearts, "],["pg",""],["ls","ws"],["ls","wh"],["hs","wd"],["at","and at least 3 diamonds (9 known cards). "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["hs","es"],["hs","eh"],["at","East will be known to have 1 spade, 5 hearts, "],["pg",""],["ls","es"],["ls","eh"],["hs","ed"],["at","and at least 3 diamonds (also 9 known cards). "],["pg",""],["ls","ed"],["hs","nc"],["hs","sc"],["at","It seems like South's play in clubs is a complete guess."],["pg",""],["ls","nc"],["ls","sc"],["nt","\nSouth can solve this problem with an unusual application of the Principle of Restricted Choice. "],["pg",""],["hs","wd"],["at","West led from a suit with 3 or 4 small cards. "],["pg",""],["ls","wd"],["hs","wc"],["at","If West had a similar holding in clubs, he may have led that suit instead. "],["pg",""],["ls","wc"],["hc","cq"],["at","West should thus be played for the @CQ.\n"],["",""]